# Dack Fayden, Helping Hand: X is the number of opponents, one here, so the enters ability reveals until it finds one
# creature card - past a Forest and an Island, both of which stay in the library - puts it onto the battlefield under
# Bot2's control (the only opponent, so no choice to make), goads it for good, and shuffles. The goad lasts for the rest
# of the game (Duration::Indefinite, not the Undercity's until-its-controller's-next-turn): it is still there on turn 6.
# Bot1 being the only other player, "attacks a player other than the one who goaded it if able" leaves nothing to choose
# from, so the goad's must-attack half has it attack Bot1 on its turns (2 life by turn 4, CR 701.15b).

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Dack Fayden, Helping Hand
Island
Island
Forest
Island
Llanowar Elves
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dack Fayden, Helping Hand.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
[T6 Bot2.DeclareAttackers]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.GoadedBy = Bot1

[Expect]
Turn = 6
Bot1.Library.Count = 10
Bot1.Battlefield = Dack Fayden, Helping Hand; Mox Jet; Mox Pearl; Mox Sapphire
Bot2.Battlefield = Llanowar Elves
Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.GoadedBy = Bot1
Bot1.Life = 18
Bot2.Life = 20
